---
name: known_sleep_location
description: >
  Campus-wide (not proximity-gated) counterpart to nearby_affordances_line's
  sleepable hint (#931 follow-up): nearby_affordances_line only names a
  sleepable arena already within the character's vision_r, so a sleepy agent
  far from a sleepable spot had no way to know where to travel until it
  happened to wander into view. Rendered by
  cognition.known_sleep_location_line() and appended only when the character
  is actually IS_SLEEPY -- an actionable answer to "where do I go", not a
  standing campus directory in every observation.
inputs:
  places:
    type: string
    description: >
      Pre-joined "<name> (<tags>)" fragments for every sleepable location in
      the game, regardless of distance, e.g.
      "Houston Hall — Reading Room (sleepable)".
sample:
  places: "Houston Hall — Reading Room (sleepable)"
---
Even if it isn't nearby, you know you can sleep at: {{ places }}.
